  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women-led trade mission in agri-food and textile sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Many barriers such as access to finance, resources and lack of viable networks contribute to women&apos;s often-lower business revenues. Ethiopian women-led business in textile, leather and agro-food processing lack the access to reliable business relationships with potential clients, partners, and suppliers. This challenge is similarly evident for women entrepreneurs who have the potential and the interest to export.The project aims to address barriers linked to social networks and business networks. The trade mission aims to support six Ethiopian women-led business to get to know the Netherlands (and European Union (EU)) market and its marketing condition and trade opportunities.The project will target those who have demonstrable capacity to enter the export market and will give them the exposure and opportunity to interact with Dutch buyers or businesses operating in the Netherlands. Moreover, the trade mission will broker deals between Dutch buyers and Ethiopian producers.</narrative>
  </description>
